message.content:
Yellow lasts only 3 s instead of the required 5 s. The trace shows EW green at 201, then EW yellow at 202-204 (3 steps), then all-red at 205. The violation records yellow duration 3 < limit 5. With `actuated=true` the controller appears to truncate the yellow phase early (possibly applying gap-out/max-green logic to yellow). Switching to fixed-time (`actuated=false`) removes the truncation and the run passes.

Triage ledger: hypothesized end-of-sim truncation ruled out because extending steps to 215 still violates at 205; actuated-induced early termination of yellow remains open and explains observations.

**Counterfactual:** disabling actuated control (single field change) makes identical-length run pass.

